About 1.5 km off La Gaulette lies Île aux Bénitiers. It is a flat coral islet of some 65 hectares once known as Île du Morne. Its beaches look straight across the lagoon to Le Morne Brabant in one of the classic views of the southwest.

There is little to do on the island itself apart from swimming and lazing in the shade and eating. That is exactly the point. Boat trips from La Gaulette and the neighbouring villages usually stop here. They often combine it with the Crystal Rock and early in the day a look for dolphins.

## Good to know

- Bring reef shoes and water and sun protection because shade is limited.
- Take all your rubbish back with you.
